From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Seer: a deleted download can be requested again

A request stays marked available after its file is deleted, and Submit reused it
as the active request, so asking again did nothing. When the item is no longer in
the library, retire the stale request and create a new one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/core/acquire/service.go new/core/acquire/service.go
index 762ed11..d5d0967 100644
--- a/core/acquire/service.go
+++ b/core/acquire/service.go
@@ -271,6 +271,11 @@ func (s *Service) Submit(ctx context.Context, userID string, item CatalogItem) (
 	if err != nil {
 		return nil, err
 	}
+	if existing != nil && existing.Status == StatusAvailable {
+		// Not in the library anymore (its file was deleted after the download): the request is stale.
+		s.setStatus(ctx, existing, StatusFailed, "file was removed from the library")
+		existing = nil
+	}
 	if existing != nil {
 		return existing, nil
 	}
